cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Taipei LULC: six-classifier comparison with cluster-aware
  validation
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite both the
  repository and the associated paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chun-ya
    family-names: Liu
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7544-929X'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ami01/taipei-lulc'
abstract: >-
  Code, sampled reflectance data, classified maps and figures
  for a comparison of six machine learning classifiers (CART,
  Random Forest, XGBoost, LightGBM, RBF support vector machine
  and a multilayer perceptron) for land use land cover mapping
  of Taipei City from Sentinel-2. The validation sample is
  drawn from hand-digitised polygons, so the split is applied
  at polygon level and every interval and hypothesis test is
  computed on the effective sample size implied by the Kish
  design effect. Under that correction none of the fifteen
  pairwise accuracy differences is significant.
keywords:
  - land use land cover
  - Sentinel-2
  - Google Earth Engine
  - machine learning
  - classification accuracy
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - effective sample size
  - Taipei
license: MIT
license-url: 'https://github.com/ami01/taipei-lulc/blob/main/LICENSE'
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      How Much Does the Classifier Matter? A Cluster-Aware
      Comparison of Six Machine Learning Algorithms for Land
      Use Land Cover Mapping of Taipei, Taiwan, Using Google
      Earth Engine and Python
    authors:
      - given-names: Chun-ya
        family-names: Liu
        orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7544-929X'
    journal: ICCK Journal of Image Analysis and Processing
